WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.350
- I'm vaxxed, yes!

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.183
- [Kelly] You look wonderful.

00:00:02.183 --> 00:00:03.780
- Oh my God, I love coming back.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.617
This is where I used to have my talk show-

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:06.810
"Chelsea Lately."
- I know.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.280
- So every time I come back here-

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.930
- Is it weird?
- some of the people

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.400
are still here, left over.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.233
- Oh.
- Yeah.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:13.290
So I get to see some of the people

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.180
that worked on my show.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.320
And then I come in,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.540
I'm here for 20 minutes,
but I get to leave, right?

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.040
- You get to leave. (laughs)
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:20.940
Yeah.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.650
- So you just got back from Mallorca?

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.550
- I went to Mallorca

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.170
for a month with a bunch-
- I've never been there.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.160
- Oh, you haven't? You have to come.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:26.993
I have a house there.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.984
- [Kelly] You did?
- Yes.

00:00:27.984 --> 00:00:29.820
And it is one of the most beautiful

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.740
places in the world, Mallorca.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.630
We went crazy.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.160
We did a lot of exercising.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.020
A little too much exercising for my own

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.170
interest, actually.
- Liking?

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.970
But we drink a lot of sangria

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.280
and then we get on our
bikes and we bike it off,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.840
so it kind of adds up.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.090
Like it makes sense so that
you can get away with it.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.620
You know what I'm saying?
- Okay. Yep.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.480
- But, like, two weeks into the vacation,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.313
my friends were like,

00:00:52.313 --> 00:00:54.429
"Are we at a fat camp? Like,
what is going on here?"

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:55.530
(audience laughing)

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.960
- So I went on a, like, a fun beach,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.220
like, whatever destination,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.847
and all of a sudden they were like,

00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:02.940
"We're going on this this
beautiful hike in the mountains."

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.750
And I was like, "This is,
like, literally it was hell.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.550
And I don't wanna do this on vacation."

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.110
I was miserable going all the way up.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:10.943
And then you get up there and you're like,

00:01:10.943 --> 00:01:12.540
"I could've just bought a postcard."

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.180
Okay, wait, so we just passed
something that you celebrate.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.080
I've never heard of this.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.460
Is it Fat Bear Week?

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.300
- Fat Bear Week.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.290
Well, I love-
- What is Fat Bear Week?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.900
- Well, Fat Bear, I think
there's a Fat Bear day

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.733
where they...

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:23.610
or is it a week?

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.540
Oh, it should be.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.180
They get the biggest,
fattest black and brown bears

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.290
and they compare their bodies.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.870
And I love big fat animals.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.020
Like my dogs are slightly obese

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.607
because I like them that way.
- Okay.

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:37.740
- And I like to get dogs that are heavier.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.420
Even if it's bad for their hips.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.462
I'll just make my house
wheelchair accessible.

00:01:41.462 --> 00:01:42.390
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.223
You know what I mean?
- With the wheels on them.

00:01:43.223 --> 00:01:44.056
- Because the more meat...

00:01:44.056 --> 00:01:46.650
I just like to get into bed
after a long day and just-

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.380
- Just cozy.
- put a big fat, furry animal

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.360
on top of me and rub my face.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.767
And then when it gets
too hot, I can just say,

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.653
"Get the hell off of me."
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:55.653 --> 00:01:56.486
You know what I mean?

00:01:56.486 --> 00:01:57.319
- Not a dude dog. (laughs)

00:01:57.319 --> 00:01:58.726
- That's what I'm looking
for in a companion.

00:01:58.726 --> 00:01:59.559
(audience applauding)

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:00.392
Yeah.
- I have Henry,

00:02:00.392 --> 00:02:01.230
that's my dog,

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.063
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:02.063 --> 00:02:02.896
- and lays right here,

00:02:02.896 --> 00:02:05.610
and thinks he's a small
dog, but not, very heavy.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.900
So I hear you're also celebrating

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.400
the end of Flip Flop season?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.080
- Oh. Oh, yeah.
- So...

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.510
- I have a problem with men in flip flops.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.947
- Oh, I have a problem with flip flops.

00:02:13.947 --> 00:02:15.630
- Oh. Oh, high five.
- Yeah.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.463
- Finally.
(hands clap)

00:02:16.463 --> 00:02:18.900
- I don't appreciate
anything between my toes.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.490
- Oh. Oh, you have a problem with...

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.280
I have a problem with other
people wearing flip flops.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.320
- I don't care what you
wanna do with your toes,

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.390
but mine shall never
have anything in them.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.290
- I feel like...

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.780
I understand what you're
saying and I respect that.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.820
I also don't like things
in between my toes,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.080
but I don't...

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.150
I think there's a season for flip flops

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.890
and that's called summertime.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.460
And you should be by, you
know, an ocean, or a beach,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.380
or a water feature when
you're wearing them.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.030
Especially if you're a straight man

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.460
who doesn't get pedicures
or take care of your feet.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.560
I don't like when men push flip flops

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.090
into other seasons

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.620
and try and get away with that.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.390
Those are shoes for women.
- Looking all unkempt.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.223
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:02:55.223 --> 00:02:56.430
- Those are for us and gay men,

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:59.160
people who take care of
their shoes and feet.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.480
Sorry, take care of their feet.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.533
- Yeah, I can't take it.
- It's also not a shoe,

00:03:02.533 --> 00:03:04.680
it's like a flop.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.360
You know, you're not supporting yourself

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.247
or protecting yourself from
all the gross things out there.

00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:10.500
- And you hear yourself coming,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.520
like, you can hear people

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.230
coming from a mile away.
- (Chelsea laughs) Yes.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.180
- Because of the flip and the flop.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.080
Like you can hear...
- Yeah.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.070
- Anyway, just say...

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.600
Okay, so it's throwback Thursday,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.800
here you are as a young woman.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.990
I love this photo. It's amazing.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.210
I have no idea you're a beauty queen!

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.121
Like it...
- Wow.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:25.954
(audience applauding)

00:03:25.954 --> 00:03:26.887
- You are...

00:03:26.887 --> 00:03:28.680
This is amazing. You are so beautiful.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.640
And I didn't know...

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.710
'Cause your personality,
you just read, like,

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.270
you would be the one to make fun maybe

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.380
or poke fun at the... (laughs)

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.960
- Exactly.
- So this is the you.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.450
- That, by the way, I was 14
years old in that picture.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.070
- You're 14 in that picture?

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.977
- And I look like I'm 65. (laughs)

00:03:42.977 --> 00:03:44.880
(audience laughing)
Well, I look like I'm 45.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.050
- You look 19.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.188
- Well, I look like the lion
king, is what I look like.

00:03:48.188 --> 00:03:49.021
(audience laughing)
But that-

00:03:49.021 --> 00:03:50.490
- Aqua Net. (laughs)
- Aqua Net, yeah.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.704
I was from New Jersey,
so that was what you did.

00:03:52.704 --> 00:03:53.670
- Texas as well.
- Every morning,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.780
you got up and made your hair

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.370
into a right angle.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.920
Yeah, no, I was in like
two beauty pageants

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.650
and then I found out
you had to have a talent

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.140
and I was like, "Ugh, you
know, what am I gonna do?"

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.750
I can't really dance and I
can't play an instrument.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.250
- Does anybody do stand-up? Does anybody-

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.527
- Well, no, not in those days.

00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:10.740
- Not then? Okay.
- Not really.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.260
I mean, not when you're 14,
that would've been a good one.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.390
But you get, like, three
minutes to show off some talent.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.867
And once I found that out, I was like,

00:04:16.867 --> 00:04:18.720
"Oh, I'll just become a model."

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.070
And then that failed miserably.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.675
So I became a stand-up comedian.

00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:23.187
(Kelly and audience laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:04:23.187 --> 00:04:26.610
- I saw that, I was like,
"Oh my gosh, it's crazy.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.443
It's beautiful."

00:04:27.443 --> 00:04:28.620
The dress is beautiful.
- Oh, well, thank you.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.880
- Yeah.
- Thank you, yeah.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.400
And pageants in the state
of New Jersey, growing up,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.070
are something that people
take very seriously.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.773
- Also in Texas.
- Yes.

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:38.280
(audience applauding)
- So, how is

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.280
the "Vaccinated and Horny" tour going?

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.780
Any favorite moments?

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.580
- Well, I just filmed
my special in Nashville,

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.413
which is the best-
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:45.413 --> 00:04:46.440
at the Ryman, you know-

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.273
- Oh my God.
- the Ryman Auditorium-

00:04:47.273 --> 00:04:48.106
- I love it.
- which is like,

00:04:48.106 --> 00:04:48.939
the best place.
(audience applauding)

00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:51.150
Yeah, so that was a highlight.
- What a cool place-

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.017
- Yeah.
- to do that.

00:04:52.017 --> 00:04:53.340
- And it looks really beautiful.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.780
And these are my last 20 dates.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.190
If you go to chelseahandler.com,

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.200
I am finishing up my tour for the year.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.160
So I'm finishing...

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.080
I'm going to all the smaller cities

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.000
that I haven't been to yet.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.190
And yeah, it's been
great to be on the road.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.920
I mean, it's great to be
able to walk into, you know,

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.290
an audience filled with
thousands of people

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.510
and bring them together, some
for the very first times,

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.740
and make them laugh.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.660
You know, remind people about togetherness

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.060
and forget about the
world that we're living in

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.050
for an hour and a half.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.034
It's a nice treat to be able to give that

00:05:21.034 --> 00:05:22.230
to these people.
- It is cool when you look out

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.270
and, 'cause at comedy
shows I find this too

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.377
and musical shows too, you're like,

00:05:26.377 --> 00:05:29.100
"Where would all these
people be at the same time?"

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:29.933
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:32.430
It's a random, you know,
motley crew of people.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.420
- Yeah.
- It's cool.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.520
- Yeah, I had a woman
at my show this weekend.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.770
I was in Niagara Falls and she was...

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.270
and I started talking
to her in the front row

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.110
and I realized she was like,

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:43.230
this 79-year-old woman
who had taken a bus in

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.740
from a town called Pickering,
which was like hours away,

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.107
and she comes to this
casino and she's like,

00:05:50.107 --> 00:05:53.100
"I lost my husband a year
ago, and I just come out

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.010
and take the bus every
few weeks to see comedy."

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.860
And I gave her my hotel room
because I wasn't staying there.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:05:59.790
And the Niagara Falls

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.960
is lit up at night-
- They always give you them.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.793
Yeah.
- and so

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:03.750
it's a beautiful view
and I was talking to her

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.190
before I knew her husband
died, I was like...

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.097
husband had died, I was like,

00:06:06.097 --> 00:06:07.440
"Oh my God, take my room.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.730
You don't have to take
the bus home tonight.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.620
Stay here, gamble, hook up,

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.540
you know, go back to my room."
(hands clapping)

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.070
And she was like this little old lady,

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.720
she had sized four-and-a-half shoes.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.970
I noticed those right away
because they were, you know,

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:18.960
little bite size.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.642
So I was like, "Mm, I like that too."

00:06:20.642 --> 00:06:23.114
(all laughing)

00:06:23.114 --> 00:06:25.350
And when she came backstage, she's like...

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.030
she told me the story about her husband.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.190
I'm like, "Oh my God, I'm so
sorry I told you to hook up."

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.207
She's like, "No, I might
actually hook up, thank you."

00:06:31.207 --> 00:06:32.460
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.440
So that was cute. That was a nice treat.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.110
She probably had no idea who
she was coming to see, so...

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.540
- But you forget though how
beautiful that is, like,

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.560
that's awesome.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.330
Like maybe there's, like,
some kind of darkness

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.163
that's happened in her life,

00:06:43.163 --> 00:06:44.730
and it's her moment to, like, escape.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:45.563
That's cool that you're like-

00:06:45.563 --> 00:06:47.340
- Yeah, I was a nice moment.
- (indistinct) escapism.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.810
- It made me feel good. Yeah, yeah.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.310
- Yeah, I like her.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.080
I hope she had a good time.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.640
So was there a moment that you knew

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.190
you were meant to do stand-up,
like, when you were young?

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.170
- You know, I would just
always go off on people

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.512
and I would like...
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:59.512 --> 00:07:00.510
- You're like Julia Sugarbaker
(both laughing)

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.520
on Designing Women.
- Yeah.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.920
I just was always arguing
with people in school.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.410
Like not other students,

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.483
but people in positions
of authority, you know?

00:07:09.483 --> 00:07:10.710
- Yeah
- Like I would always just...

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:11.880
Everyone would just annoy me.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.770
I'm like, "Why does this guy
get to tell me what to do?

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.760
because I'm eight?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.593
You know, this is like,

00:07:15.593 --> 00:07:17.457
I don't like this paradigm."

00:07:18.695 --> 00:07:21.180
And so when I got older and I moved to LA,

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.770
I didn't really know what I was gonna do.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.780
I thought I'd become an
actress or something,

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.490
and then I would read other people's lines

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.040
and I wasn't very good
at reading other things

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.090
that people had written.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.100
Like I wanted to write my own material.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.840
And then somebody suggested it.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.240
They were like, "You should do stand-up."

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.530
And I was like, "Huh."

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.510
I'm like, "Me on stage with a microphone

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.160
and nobody else is allowed to talk."

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:41.993
I'm like,
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:41.993 --> 00:07:43.410
"That's exactly what I should do."

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.377
- This is my calling.
- I'm like,

00:07:44.377 --> 00:07:47.190
"That sounds like a plan
I could get behind."

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.750
But I was so scared, you know.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.200
Because getting up on stage
in front of everybody,

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.480
as you know, is scary.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.460
And talking is scary,

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.570
so it took a while.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.940
I mean, you got a lot of diarrhea.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:00.900
I mean, that's what happens.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:01.733
- And I'm telling you-
- Lot of nerves.

00:08:01.733 --> 00:08:03.450
- there's a very big difference
of what you just said.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.283
'Cause people are like,

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.910
"You sing in front of people
all the time, like why..."

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.490
'Cause sometimes I don't
ever get nervous doing this

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:09.840
or like talking like this,

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.190
but when they ask me to, like, present

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.090
or, like, do something like that

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.740
or I have to talk in it,

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.109
literally, my stomach is just
like (mimics stomach rumbling)

00:08:16.109 --> 00:08:17.010
(Chelsea laughs)
Like, it's just like what...

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.120
'Cause it's so different.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.550
Because with music, I feel
like there's melody, there's...

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:24.210
You're locked into, like, a
formula of what's happening,

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.340
and you're just out there on your own.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.450
Like your own timing,

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.190
the crowd's different, they
laugh at different thing.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.023
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:30.023 --> 00:08:30.870
You're feeding off different energy.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.770
That's way harder.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.030
- Yeah, it is. It is.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.410
But once you get good at it,

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.570
and once you have an audience and fans

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.470
that are so loyal and come to see you,

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.403
it becomes this-
- Cathartic kind of thing?

00:08:41.403 --> 00:08:42.810
- It's just awesome.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.070
It's awesome to get out there

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.990
and just like destroy it, you know.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.013
Like go out there
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:47.013 --> 00:08:48.270
(hand clapping)
and crush the show

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.090
and get a standing ovation.
(audience applauding)

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:50.940
- Feels good.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.890
- And just watching people's reactions

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.960
to the crazy things that
come out of your mouth,

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.030
you're watching people go, "Oh my God."

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.800
You know, like, it gives me joy

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.840
to bring that emotion to people.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.280
- I love that it still does that.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.329
- Yeah, I know.
- That's so cool.

00:09:03.329 --> 00:09:04.410
- I know.
- Yeah.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.790
- You know, sometimes it doesn't

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.410
and sometimes you have
to bring back the joy

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.180
in a performance.
- Me too.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.820
- So you know, you have to
get be in your flow state.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:12.960
So you always have to remember

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:15.870
that you're performing for your
audience, not for yourself.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.250
- Yeah. Amen.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.715
You have had a lot of therapy.

00:09:18.715 --> 00:09:19.947
It's nice.
(Chelsea laughs)

00:09:19.947 --> 00:09:20.780
It's nice.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.140
It's breast cancer awareness month.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.850
I know that you lost your
mama to breast cancer.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:27.480
So what's something that she
taught you that stays with you?

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.330
- Well, she told me to
always wear my seatbelt.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.300
So I always do that even when
I don't feel like I should,

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.760
or that I don't need to,
I always wear my seatbelt.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.510
But I did get my mammogram
the other day for...

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.343
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:39.330
'Cause Katie Courick and I,

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.460
she said, "Would you post about, you know,

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.510
breast cancer awareness?"

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.500
And I said, "Of course."

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.540
And then I went and got my mammogram

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.230
and I was just thinking,
like, "What do people do..."

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.320
'Cause men have to get tested
for breast cancer as well.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.260
And what do men do in those
machines that trap you like that

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.670
when they don't have any breast tissue

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.550
to put in there, you know?

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.983
- Yeah, what does it squeeze, yeah?

00:09:59.983 --> 00:10:00.816
- I don't know.

00:10:00.816 --> 00:10:03.780
But it must be so painful,
you know, to put, I mean...

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.430
I don't really know where
I'm going with this story,

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:06.390
but I was just...
- No, but I'll tell you, like,

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.160
people kinda scared me
about getting a mammogram

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.190
and I've had a couple of
them and I don't feel...

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.290
It didn't bother me, but I
mean, I guess I have a boob

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.730
so it might hurt if you don't have a boob.

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:16.950
- Yeah, I mean, I have very large breasts

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.450
and it hurts badly, so...

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.320
- I don't.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.153
- Okay, well that's... (laughs)

00:10:20.153 --> 00:10:23.460
- I've just a really good,
okay amount and it's really...

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.390
it served me well.
(hands clapping)

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.920
- Yeah.
- In mammograms. (laughs)

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.167
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:10:27.167 --> 00:10:29.880
'Cause it's not that
unpleasant, it's bearable-

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:30.980
but it's unpleasant,
- No, my sister is like you.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.250
- is a good word for it, yeah,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.083
I would describe it as unpleasant.

00:10:33.083 --> 00:10:34.530
- It's so smart though,
'cause people are...

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.030
women are getting younger and younger.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.800
- Yeah, you have to always
take care of yourself

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.300
and you have to get breast exams

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.700
and you have to get
colonoscopies at the age of 45.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.730
And they both don't sound
appealing and they're not,

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.350
but it's just good to get ahead

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:49.200
and have information about
anything that might go wrong.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.033
You know-
- Yeah, to catch it.

00:10:50.033 --> 00:10:50.866
- in your health world.

00:10:50.866 --> 00:10:52.215
You wanna be ahead of it, of course.

00:10:52.215 --> 00:10:53.048
- Absolutely.
- Knowledge is power.

00:10:53.048 --> 00:10:54.443
(audience applauding)
- Yep.

